   {"issue": "Subsection F makes \"just cause\" include, \"as determined by the University,\" conduct \"seriously prejudicial to the best interests of the University,\" conduct that \"brings the University into disrepute,\" or that reflects \"moral turpitude\" — each an unmeasured standard, and the self-judging phrase makes it unclear whether the University's determination is conclusive or reviewable. This is the language on which a wrongful-termination dispute would turn.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.81},
